Keep a shared matrix as empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared deepest as 0.
For every spot from 0 to 15.
Place 0 into matrix.

Set item 4 of matrix to 1.
Set item 1 of matrix to 1.
Set item 6 of matrix to 1.
Set item 9 of matrix to 1.
Set item 7 of matrix to 1.
Set item 13 of matrix to 1.
The heights is a list of 4 zeros.
To walk from node (a whole number) with parent (a whole number) and depth (a whole number).
If depth is more than deepest, set deepest to depth.
For every other from 0 to 3.
The at is node times 4 plus other.
If item at of matrix is 1 and other is not parent.
Walk from other with node and depth plus 1.

For every root from 0 to 3.
Set deepest to 0.
Walk from root with -1 and 0.
Set item root of heights to deepest.

The best is item 0 of heights.
For every root from 1 to 3.
If item root of heights is less than best, set best to item root of heights.

For every root from 0 to 3.
If item root of heights is best, show root.
